Subject: [PATCH] spi: ingenic: clear the SSICDR gate before hardware setup
Upstream-Status: Pending

Clear bit 27 of SSICDR through a direct register access before programming
the SSI controller. This is a workaround for the source-clock gate not
being cleared by clk_prepare_enable.

diff --git a/drivers/spi/spi-ingenic.c b/drivers/spi/spi-ingenic.c
index 44535539f1e1497098401415edc7bf5e58d7d4e5..851022215eb0a5848f3fd867980593d8c5aa01c9 100644
--- a/drivers/spi/spi-ingenic.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi-ingenic.c
@@ -317,6 +317,9 @@ static int spi_ingenic_prepare_hardware(struct spi_controller *ctlr)
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
+// Hack to write SSICDR - should have been done by clk_prepare_enable(priv->clk)
+*((volatile uint32_t *) 0xb000005c) &= ~(1U << 27);
+
 	regmap_write(priv->map, REG_SSICR0, REG_SSICR0_EACLRUN);
 	regmap_write(priv->map, REG_SSICR1, 0);
 	regmap_write(priv->map, REG_SSISR, 0);
